# ss-queue

Scout failing tests and/or open tickets and build/refresh the swarm candidate queue with wave assignments.

## Purpose

Produces a dated queue file and updates the primary queue file — an ordered list of fixable failures for the next swarm wave. Each entry contains a bounded hypothesis, source file footprint, reference-implementation analog, and wave assignment. All project-specific parameters come from the **queue brief file**, not from this skill.

## Invocation

```
/ss-queue [<brief-path>] [source=<tests|tickets|both>] [<section>]
```

- `<brief-path>` — path to the swarm brief. If omitted, auto-discover the unique `docs/swarm-lanes/swarm-brief*.md` in cwd. Any arg containing `/` or ending in `.md` is treated as the brief path.
- `source` — discovery source (default: `tests`):
  - `tests` — run the test suite and scout failures (original mode)
  - `tickets` — evaluate open tickets from the ticket system
  - `both` — run both discovery paths and merge results
- `<section>` — for `source=tests`: section name(s) to sweep, or `all` (default). Ignored for `source=tickets`.

Examples:
```
/ss-queue                                          # tests, all sections
/ss-queue source=tickets                           # evaluate open tickets
/ss-queue source=both css-flexbox                  # tickets + flex section
/ss-queue docs/swarm-lanes/swarm-brief-lou.md source=tickets
```

