## Discovery: from-tickets

*Used when `source=tickets` or `source=both`.*

This path evaluates open (unstarted) tickets from the ticket system as potential queue candidates. It uses a **two-tier review**: fast haiku agents apply the checklist mechanically; the orchestrator (sonnet) reviews uncertain verdicts and makes final calls.

### K1 — Fetch candidate tickets

Fetch tickets from the ticket system with:
- Team/prefix from brief
- States: the brief's `Ticket states to evaluate` (typically `Backlog`, `Todo`)

Exclude:
- Tickets already in the existing queue (match on ticket ID or `area`+`label`)
- Tickets whose area is covered by an In Progress ticket (loaded in Step 0b)
- Tickets with no hypothesis or file footprint in their description (obviously incomplete)

### K2 — Launch haiku evaluation swarm via Workflow

One haiku agent per ticket, all in parallel (`model: haiku`).

**What each haiku evaluator does** — provide it with:
- The full ticket description (title + body)
- The scout criteria verbatim from the brief
- The brief's reference SHA and hard rules
- The project's source tree location and Go command

**Haiku evaluator task:**

> You are evaluating a ticket as a potential swarm queue candidate. Apply the scout criteria
> checklist below mechanically. Your job is to return a structured verdict — not prose.
>
> **Step 1 — Check each scout criterion:**
> For each criterion in the brief's `Scout criteria`, mark it pass/fail/unknown based solely
> on what is in the ticket description. Do not speculate; if the ticket is silent on a
> criterion, mark it `unknown`.
>
> **Step 2 — Verify the file footprint against current source:**
> The ticket may have been filed weeks or months ago. For each file named in the ticket:
> - Check that the file still exists at that path.
> - Grep for the key symbol or mechanism named in the hypothesis.
> - If the code has already been fixed (the mechanism no longer exists), mark criterion 1
>   as `fail` with reason "already implemented."
>
> **Step 3 — Verify the target test still fails:**
> Run the specific target test from the ticket using the brief's `Target test` command.
> A test that now passes is no longer a valid candidate — mark it `already_fixed`.
>
> **Step 4 — Return verdict:**
> - `pass` — all criteria pass, test still fails, file footprint verified
> - `fail` — one or more criteria definitively fail (record which and why)
> - `uncertain` — one or more criteria are `unknown` OR the hypothesis looks plausible
>   but you cannot confirm the root cause without deeper analysis
> - `already_fixed` — the target test now passes; no work needed

**Haiku evaluator output schema:**

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["ticket_id", "verdict", "criteria_results", "candidate"],
  "properties": {
    "ticket_id":       { "type": "string" },
    "verdict":         { "type": "string", "enum": ["pass", "fail", "uncertain", "already_fixed"] },
    "confidence":      { "type": "string", "enum": ["high", "medium", "low"] },
    "fail_reasons":    { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
    "criteria_results": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "criterion": { "type": "string" },
          "result":    { "type": "string", "enum": ["pass", "fail", "unknown"] },
          "note":      { "type": "string" }
        }
      }
    },
    "code_still_matches": { "type": "boolean", "description": "true if the source files still show the described gap" },
    "test_still_fails":   { "type": "boolean" },
    "candidate": {
      "description": "Populated on pass or uncertain — the queue entry to add if accepted",
      "type": ["object", "null"],
      "properties": {
        "area":               { "type": "string" },
        "label":              { "type": "string" },
        "status":             { "type": "string", "enum": ["ready", "flagged", "blocked", "defer"] },
        "source_ticket":      { "type": "string", "description": "Ticket ID this candidate was derived from" },
        "tests":              { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
        "hypothesis":         { "type": "string" },
        "reference_analog":   { "type": "object", "properties": { "file": {"type":"string"}, "symbol": {"type":"string"}, "sha": {"type":"string"} } },
        "primary_files":      { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
        "also_touches":       { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } },
        "estimated_diff_pct": { "type": ["number", "null"] },
        "confidence":         { "type": "string", "enum": ["high", "medium", "low"] },
        "reject_reason":      { "type": ["string", "null"] },
        "blocker_ticket":     { "type": ["string", "null"] }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### K3 — Orchestrator review of uncertain verdicts

After the haiku swarm returns:

**Automatic decisions (no human needed):**
- `pass` + `confidence=high` → accept the candidate as-is
- `fail` → discard; log the `fail_reasons`
- `already_fixed` → discard; note it in the report as a stale ticket to close

**Orchestrator review required:**
- `pass` + `confidence=medium` or `low` → orchestrator reads the ticket + haiku report and decides: accept / reject / accept-with-modifications
- `uncertain` → orchestrator reads the ticket, reviews the criteria results, does any additional source-reading needed, and makes the call
- Any verdict where `code_still_matches=false` or `test_still_fails=false` contradicts the expected result → investigate before accepting

The orchestrator records its decision for each reviewed ticket: `accepted`, `rejected` (with reason), or `modified` (with what changed in the candidate).

